#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# bit_xor

#% text
# `bit_xor(n1, n2, ...)` gives the bitwise exclusive or of the integers.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Negative integers are taken in two's complement. `bit_xor()` is 0. `bit_xor` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
bit_xor(12, 10)
#% output
#= 6

#% cell
bit_xor(5, 5)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
bit_xor(1, 2, 3)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
bit_xor(-1, 6)
#% output
#= -7

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# Swapping two numbers without a third:

#% cell
a = 13; b = 29; a = bit_xor(a, b); b = bit_xor(a, b); a = bit_xor(a, b); [a, b]
#% output
#= [29, 13]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `xor` is `or` minus `and`:

#% cell
[bit_xor(37, 22), bit_or(37, 22) - bit_and(37, 22)]
#% output
#= [51, 51]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `bit_and`, `bit_or`, `bit_not`
